# No Em Dashes

Never use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) anywhere: UI copy, comments,
docs, commit messages, or any generated text. This applies to every update.

Also avoid the en dash (`–`, U+2013) as a substitute for punctuation.

## What to use instead

Rewrite the sentence with standard punctuation:

- A comma for a light pause
- A period or semicolon to split into two clauses
- A colon before a list or explanation
- Parentheses for an aside
- A regular hyphen (`-`) only for compound words (e.g. `AI-driven`)

## Examples

```
// BAD
I build AI agents — automating complex workflows.
Interactive workshops for product teams—from prototyping to production.

// GOOD
I build AI agents, automating complex workflows.
Interactive workshops for product teams, from prototyping to production.
```

When editing existing files, also remove any em dashes you encounter.
